/*Q16.
Imagine adventurers going on a big journey through two different worlds. They have a special Adventure Planner's Time Tracker to keep track of their time. They just need to tell the Tracker how many Earth days they spent on two different worlds.

In this adventure, one day in World 1 is like 2 Earth days. But in World 2, one day is only half an Earth day.

Your job is to figure out the total number of Earth days the adventurers spent traveling in both worlds.

Input Format:
  - The first line contains an integer representing the number of days spent in World 1.
  - The second line contains an integer representing the number of days spent in World 2.

Output Format:
  - The result is the total Earth days as a decimal number that displays up to one decimal place.

Note: A partial code is provided in the editor.*/
///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
/*Logic: 1 day in World 1 = 2 Earth days, 1 day in World 2 = 0.5. Print to one decimal place.*/
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int world1 = sc.nextInt();
        int world2 = sc.nextInt();
        double total = world1 * 2.0 + world2 * 0.5;
        System.out.printf("%.1f%n", total);
        sc.close();
    }
}

